  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Neoisostegane may interact with SNB-78 through a series of target-mediated pathways. Specifically, Neoisostegane is implicated in targeting the mitochondrial thioredoxin, which is a target of Spathelia bischromene and Yuanhunine, both of which also target SNB-78. This indicates a potential multi-step interaction where Neoisostegane may influence the activity of these intermediaries, ultimately affecting SNB-78. The scores from the three paths, though slightly varying, all point to a consistent relationship, suggesting that Neoisostegane may modulate the activity of thioredoxin-related molecules, which in turn influence SNB-78. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Neoisostegane and SNB-78, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated."
